ight_project_visibility.py) given the tree keeps its directory names.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.79,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 8: 'by-path helpers become `import_module`; `sys.modules` seeds, namespace stubs, engine-dir constants and `sys.path.insert` go'","Plan: 'Test dirs tests/{unit,integration}/rebar_reconciler/ keep their names (next story).'","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_store_unbind.py:23 `_SRC_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3] / 'src' / 'rebar' / '_engine' / 'rebar_reconciler'` then `spec_from_file_location(name, _SRC_DIR / filename)` — this `.../_engine/rebar_reconciler` directory ceases to exist after `git mv`; the idiom repeats across ~100+ files (test_fetch_multi_project, test_link_mapping, apply/test_applier*, diffing/*, state/*, mutate/*, …)","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_try_load_step_sys_modules.py:10 `MAIN_PATH = REPO_ROOT / 'src' / 'rebar' / '_engine' / 'rebar_reconciler' / '__main__.py'` and :37 `assert 'rebar_reconciler.applier' in sys.modules`","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_preflight_project_visibility.py:29 `MAIN_PATH = ENGINE_DIR / 'rebar_reconciler' / '__main__.py'` and :51 `spec_from_file_location('rebar_reconciler.__main__', MAIN_PATH)`"],"finding":"The `git mv` of the `rebar_reconciler` package invalidates the hard-coded `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` source paths and `rebar_reconciler.*` spec names used by ~100+ by-path test loaders under `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/`, but the plan's enumerated test-change inventory (steps 2/4/8) names only a handful of orchestrate/`_engine_module`/`MODE_CAPS` files and otherwise relies on a blanket 'by-path helpers become import_module' rule. Two concrete files that break are not named: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_try_load_step_sys_modules.py` (MAIN_PATH = `.../_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`, asserts `sys.modules['rebar_reconciler.applier']`) and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_preflight_project_visibility.py` (MAIN_PATH at the old dir, spec name `rebar_reconciler.__main__`). These are string path/key references the LSP cannot resolve, so a symbol-graph sweep alone would miss them.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f407a482605d76b65","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Step 8 ('Tests: by-path helpers become import_module … Test dirs tests/{unit,integration}/rebar_reconciler/ keep their names') and the Testing gate 'pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler … -q'","norm_id":"n94366bfae1466368","priority":0.11,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_try_load_step_sys_modules.py: `spec_from_file_location(..., MAIN_PATH)` points at the moved-away `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py` and asserts `sys.modules['rebar_reconciler.applier']` — collection/assertion fails after the move; not in the plan's inventory.","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_preflight_project_visibility.py: MAIN_PATH at `.../_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py` and spec name `rebar_reconciler.__main__` both go stale; `main_mod` fixture fails `MAIN_PATH.exists()` for the whole module.","The ~100+ `_SRC_DIR`/`_REC`/`RECON_DIR`/`APPLIER_PATH`/`DISPATCH_PATH` constants pointing at `.../_engine/rebar_reconciler/<filename>` resolve to a nonexistent directory, collect-erroring the `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` gate the plan requires to pass."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","p